 "answer": "**Possibly, but don’t count on clear air tomorrow, Sunday, October 18.** Singapore’s National Environment Agency expects showers and shifting winds to reduce haze arriving from Kalimantan over the weekend. It also warns that smoke from Sumatra may still reach Singapore. Its latest published PSI forecast is for **Saturday**, not Sunday, so there isn’t yet a firm air-quality forecast for tomorrow. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf you’re planning to be outdoors, check NEA’s next-day PSI forecast when it’s issued. Before heading out, check the **1-hour PM₂.₅ reading** for the conditions at that time. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026?utm_source=openai))",
